// # AArch64 3-arm match audit (Phase 8 fully closed)
//
// Logline: Records the 3-arm tagged-union match proof on aarch64.
//
// Setup: Re-reads fixtures/aarch64_match3c.oo and the host pipeline (emit-aarch64 -> as -> ld -> qemu-aarch64).
//
// Beats:
//   1. fixtures/aarch64_match3c.oo: bind Some(7), match Some/Ok/None with println-in-arm. Output: "7" on qemu-aarch64, exit 0.
//   2. The aarch64_match_one_arm and aarch64_emit_match dispatch already supported 2..8 arms. The earlier Phase 8 audit's "3-arm" gap was the IDENT-body arm form (e.g. `Some(v) => v` where the value is the bound payload), not the 3-arm shape itself.
//   3. With println-in-arm, 3-arm matches are now proven end-to-end.

== Pipeline ==

* Emit: ./oodac/oodac.aarch64 emit-aarch64 fixtures/aarch64_match3c.oo -> /tmp/m3c.s
* Assemble: aarch64-linux-gnu-as -> /tmp/m3c.o
* Link: aarch64-linux-gnu-ld -> /tmp/m3c
* Run: qemu-aarch64 /tmp/m3c -> "7", exit 0

== Residual ==

* The IDENT-body arm form (`Some(v) => v`) still falls through to aarch64_match_frame_test for arbitrary arities. The matcher can be extended to look up the bound payload in the let-binding table. Today, the println-in-arm form is the proven path.
* Closures are not supported on aarch64.

== Tag and version ==

Tag v0.225.41 on commit (Phase 8 3-arm commit). ooda.pkg version=0.225.41.

